{%- comment -%}
  Montibello PDP — UNDER shade browser.

  The 57 UNDER shades are NOT 27 Shopify variants (per
  docs/shopify-product-architecture.md) — they are `montibello_under_shade`
  metaobjects referenced by the informational `under-permanent-colour`
  product's `montibello.shades` metafield. This section only ever renders on
  that one PDP (any other product simply has no `shades` value and the
  section stays hidden). Shades are grouped by `shade_family` to match the
  official colour-chart presentation. A shade renders its real swatch color
  only when one was authored on the metaobject — never a guessed or
  generated hex value; without one it shows a neutral placeholder chip with
  just the code, which is still useful as a chart reference. A shade is
  hidden only when its `active` field is explicitly set to false — left
  blank/unset, it is treated as active, since the field is an opt-out flag
  for retiring a shade, not an opt-in gate.

  Fields are accessed with direct dot notation (`shade.shade_family.value`),
  not `shade.fields.shade_family.value`. Family grouping and the "at least
  one active shade in this family" check use plain `for`/`if` loops rather
  than a `where: 'fields....value'` filter, which is not a supported pattern
  for metaobject reference lists.

  IMPORTANT — Liquid reference-resolution cap (confirmed live via `shopify
  theme console`): `product.metafields.montibello.shades.value` truncates
  to the first 50 resolved metaobjects the instant a list.metaobject_reference
  field is dereferenced — upstream of any `for`/`limit`/`offset` tag, so a
  single field can never expose more than 50 objects to Liquid no matter how
  the loop over it is written. `montibello.shades` therefore holds only the
  first 50 canonical shades (indices 0-49); the remaining 7 live in a second
  metafield, `montibello.shades_overflow` (<=50 items, so it resolves in
  full). Both metafields reference the exact same 57 canonical
  `montibello_under_shade` metaobjects authored originally; nothing was
  duplicated or deleted. See
  scripts/shopify/under-shades-overflow-split-apply.js for how the split was
  produced (idempotent, re-derivable from the original 57-reference list at
  any time).

  Every pass below runs over BOTH fields in sequence (`shades_primary` then
  `shades_overflow`) rather than merging them into one array first —
  `| concat:` was tried and confirmed (via a live debug render) to silently
  return a blank/unusable result when given two already-resolved
  metaobject-reference arrays, so this dual-loop form is what's actually
  proven working, not a theoretical shortcut.

  GRID VISIBILITY (UNDER 4-PDP official parity pass, P0 #3): the official
  permanent-colour PDP does NOT render an inline 57-circle swatch grid — it
  shows only the "CARTA DE COLOR" download CTA (confirmed live). The grid
  itself stays fully implemented here (not deleted) behind a new
  `show_grid` setting, default true, so the browsable chart can still be
  placed elsewhere later (e.g. a dedicated colour-chart page) without
  rebuilding it.

  CTA RELOCATION (UNDER final punctual fix): the download CTA that used to
  render here was moved INTO sections/montibello-product-benefits.liquid's
  own lifestyle photo-row, directly under its 4 result lines, so it reads
  as part of that block instead of a separate section with its own
  background. The product template instance now leaves both `file_url`
  blank and `show_grid: false`, so this section has nothing left to show —
  `has_visible_content` below keeps it from rendering an empty padded
  band in that case. The grid-rendering code itself is untouched and still
  works exactly as before if `show_grid`/`file_url` are ever set again on
  this section (e.g. for a dedicated colour-chart page).
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  assign shades_primary = product.metafields.montibello.shades.value
  assign shades_overflow = product.metafields.montibello.shades_overflow.value
  assign has_shades = false
  for shade in shades_primary
    assign has_shades = true
    break
  endfor
  unless has_shades
    for shade in shades_overflow
      assign has_shades = true
      break
    endfor
  endunless

  if section.settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id
  endif
%}

{% liquid
  assign show_grid = true
  if section.settings.show_grid == false
    assign show_grid = false
  endif

  assign has_visible_content = false
  if show_grid or section.settings.file_url != blank or section.settings.heading != blank
    assign has_visible_content = true
  endif
%}

{% if has_shades and has_visible_content %}
  <div
    class="section-background{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
  ></div>
  <div
    class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }}{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %} montibello-shade-browser spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  >
    {% if section.settings.heading != blank %}
      <h2 class="montibello-shade-browser__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    {% endif %}

    {% if section.settings.file_url != blank %}
      <div class="montibello-shade-browser__file-link-wrap">
        <a class="montibello-shade-browser__file-link" href="{{ section.settings.file_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <span class="montibello-shade-browser__file-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18">
              <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-4m4-5l5 5 5-5m-5 5V3"></path>
            </svg>
          </span>
          {{ section.settings.file_label | default: 'Descargar Carta de Color' }}
        </a>
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if show_grid %}
      {% comment %}
        Discover distinct family names, without using `.size` or `where` —
        just a string-marker accumulator over plain dot-notation field
        access, run across both fields so no shade is missed.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% assign seen_family_markers = '' %}
      {% assign family_name_string = '' %}
      {% for shade in shades_primary %}
        {% assign family = shade.shade_family.value | default: 'Otros' %}
        {% assign marker = '|' | append: family | append: '|' %}
        {% unless seen_family_markers contains marker %}
          {% assign seen_family_markers = seen_family_markers | append: marker %}
          {% assign family_name_string = family_name_string | append: family | append: '||' %}
        {% endunless %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% for shade in shades_overflow %}
        {% assign family = shade.shade_family.value | default: 'Otros' %}
        {% assign marker = '|' | append: family | append: '|' %}
        {% unless seen_family_markers contains marker %}
          {% assign seen_family_markers = seen_family_markers | append: marker %}
          {% assign family_name_string = family_name_string | append: family | append: '||' %}
        {% endunless %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% assign family_name_list = family_name_string | split: '||' %}

      {% for family_name in family_name_list %}
        {% assign family_has_active_shade = false %}
        {% for shade in shades_primary %}
          {% assign shade_family = shade.shade_family.value | default: 'Otros' %}
          {% if shade_family == family_name and shade.active.value != false %}
            {% assign family_has_active_shade = true %}
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        {% for shade in shades_overflow %}
          {% assign shade_family = shade.shade_family.value | default: 'Otros' %}
          {% if shade_family == family_name and shade.active.value != false %}
            {% assign family_has_active_shade = true %}
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}

        {% if family_has_active_shade %}
          <h3 class="montibello-shade-browser__family">{{ family_name }}</h3>
          <div class="montibello-shade-browser__grid">
            {% for shade in shades_primary %}
              {% assign shade_family = shade.shade_family.value | default: 'Otros' %}
              {% if shade_family == family_name and shade.active.value != false %}
                {% render 'montibello-pdp-shade-chip', shade: shade %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
            {% for shade in shades_overflow %}
              {% assign shade_family = shade.shade_family.value | default: 'Otros' %}
              {% if shade_family == family_name and shade.active.value != false %}
                {% render 'montibello-pdp-shade-chip', shade: shade %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
{% endif %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .montibello-shade-browser__heading {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto 24px;
    padding-inline: 20px;
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 700;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding-inline: 30px;
    }
  }

  /* BLACK FILLED CTA (UNDER FINAL 20/20 MICRO-POLISH): was a plain
     underlined text link, floating in a visually separate, differently-
     shaded block well below the editorial rows — the official page shows
     a solid black button sitting immediately under the last result row,
     inside the same flow. Restyled as a real filled button (was: inline
     text + `text-decoration: underline`); the section's own top padding
     was also dropped to 0 in the template instance so this renders flush
     against the editorial section above instead of a detached band. */
  .montibello-shade-browser__file-link-wrap {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 20px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding-inline: 30px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__file-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    padding: 16px 28px;
    background-color: #111111;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__file-link:hover {
    background-color: #000000;
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__file-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__family {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 32px auto 12px;
    padding-inline: 20px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    opacity: 0.7;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding-inline: 30px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__family:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 20px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    /* `width: 100%` is load-bearing, not decorative: a grid container's
       `width: auto` can resolve to its own `max-width` instead of the
       viewport-derived containing-block width — confirmed live at 390px,
       where this produced a computed width of exactly 1400px and
       `auto-fill` laid out 14 columns, overflowing the page. `min(84px,
       100%)` alone (a track-size floor) does not fix this: the bug is in
       how many tracks `auto-fill` decides to create, not in any single
       track's width. */
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(84px, 100%), 1fr));

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding-inline: 30px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__chip {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__swatch {
    display: block;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-background-secondary, #ece7dc);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border, #e4dfd4);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  /* This is a reference colour chart, not a variant picker — no click
     selection exists — but a hover affordance still helps the swatch
     grid read as an intentional, browsable UI rather than a flat list. */
  .montibello-shade-browser__chip:hover .montibello-shade-browser__swatch {
    transform: scale(1.12);
    border-color: var(--color-foreground, #2e2d2c);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
  }

  .montibello-shade-browser__code {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: center;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Carta de Color",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Título",
      "default": "Carta de Color"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "file_url",
      "label": "URL del PDF (Carta de Color)",
      "info": "Reutiliza el mismo asset ya aprobado en la página de colección UNDER — no subir un PDF nuevo.",
      "default": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0874/8479/3025/files/montibello-under-carta-de-color.pdf?v=1789594566"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "file_label",
      "label": "Texto del enlace",
      "default": "Descargar Carta de Color"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_grid",
      "label": "Mostrar cuadrícula de tonos",
      "info": "Desactivado en el PDP oficial — la página oficial solo muestra el botón de descarga, no la cuadrícula de círculos.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "Color de fondo"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "Ancho de sección",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page-width", "label": "Ancho de página" },
        { "value": "full-width", "label": "Ancho completo" }
      ],
      "default": "page-width"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Superior",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Inferior",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
